KZ3 patch 2202 (RSX pass 173): RSX_VIEWS=1, the split-screen per-view counter (diagnostic, default off).
Per flip that had draws, one `[views] flip=N views=V draws=D words=W binds=B surf=S scis=C hist=0:a 1:b 2:c 3+:d | v0 WxH
rect=x0,y0-x1,y1 draws=.. words=.. binds=.. | v1 ... | rest draws=.. words=.. binds=.. tail_words=..` line on stderr; after
RSX_VIEWS_N lines (default 100) only a hist line every 300 flips. RSX_VIEWS_MIN = draw packets a rect needs to count as a
view (default 8).
View boundary signal: the guest scissor (NV4097 SET_SCISSOR 0x08C0/0x08C4) read at each draw packet (sink_draw_arrays,
sink_draw_index, sink_inline_array). Both views of a split screen draw into the same colour/zeta targets (so a target
change does not separate them), the port's draw viewport is always the whole surface, and the game's per-view loop
(SceneRenderer::RenderFrame 0x1F5030) is PPU code that the RSX command stream does not carry, so the walker cannot see its
markers. The scissor is the one per-view state in the stream. Draws are grouped by (target size, clamped scissor rect);
view-like = >= RSX_VIEWS_MIN draws and >= 25 % of the target area; the largest set of pairwise non-overlapping view-like
rects within one target size is the view set (light and UI scissors are small, shadow maps and post targets are other
sizes). Surface/zeta change count (surf) and scissor change count (scis) are logged as the alternative signals. Method words
(rsx_live_draw_method entries) are attributed to the next draw; enabled fragment texture units per draw are the binds.
libs/video/rsx_views.h is pure C (host test tools/smoke/test_views.sh: 1, 2 and 3-view synthetic streams and negative
controls); the instance and RSX_VIEWS switch live in cellGcmSys.c beside g_rsx_o0 (enabled at walk-pass begin); the hooks are in
rsx_live_draw.c only (rsx_live_draw_method for the words, the three draw-packet sinks, sink_flip), so host tests that link
rsx_dispatch.c alone are unaffected. Off: one
predicted-not-taken test of g_rsx_views.on per method word, draw packet and flip. ASSUMPTION (not run in the game): views
do not overlap and each covers >= 25 % of the target.

